# Limits and unverified behavior

This is a Dirty Mode source construction. No dependencies were installed, no application/test/benchmark was run, no GitHub workflow ran and no provider was called. Runtime behavior and hostile-input containment remain unverified.

The README extractor deliberately recognizes explicit static sentence forms. Examples include “The function `present` is declared in module `sample`.”, “The file `src/example.py` exists.”, “The config key `project.version` equals `\"0.1.0\"`.”, “The dependency `requests` with constraint `>=2` is declared.”, “The project requires-python is `>=3.12`.”, “The CLI entry `tool` maps to `package:main`.” and “The environment variable `API_HOST` is referenced.” Supported bounded forms name `async def`, literal defaults/constants/decorator arguments, or explicit raise syntax. Other wording is retained with an unknown reason. Supported static syntax does not establish availability, correctness, compatibility, security or performance.

Conjunctions and conditions remain unresolved unless a future extractor preserves every qualifier during decomposition. Code fences only provide explicit import binding context; their examples are not automatically claims. Original source blocks and unmapped ranges remain in the inventory. An incomplete parser or scope cannot justify absence. CommonMark line maps select blocks; raw bytes remain authoritative for quotes, CRLF and Unicode coordinates.

Snapshot/Git isolation, path replacement defenses, parser memory/time enforcement, negative-query replay and citation integrity are constructed source controls whose effectiveness has not been exercised. The tool should fail closed where enforcement is unavailable. A static source inspection is not a security proof.

Reports are local artifacts containing source excerpts. The static HTML escapes all source text, has no scripts or external resources, and does not render README HTML/links. Reopening reports must use the exact frozen snapshot, never current HEAD. This containment remains runtime unverified.

Evaluation is not measured. Source provides descriptive counts, failure denominators, a conservative packet path baseline, whole-family bootstrap calculation and unknown-aware attempt summaries. Actual human labels, independent corpus custody, heldout access restrictions, paired-arm inference integration, live extraction/single-pass calls, measured intervals, resolved model/context identities, cost and latency measurements remain absent. No superiority, accuracy or hiring-value claim is made.

There is no CI/deployment scaffolding in this Dirty Mode increment. The actual exact-revision self/fixture GitHub Action and independent nonauthoring product acceptance remain required after activation. No public release is authorized.
